-- title:
--   Analytic extension across τ of a function regular at P_τ
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a positive integer and let $D$ be a complex place dictionary of level $N$: a point map $\tau \mapsto P_\tau$ from $\mathbb{H}$ to the places of the field $\mathbb{C}F_N :=$ `laurentBaseChange ℂ (modularFunctionFieldFull N)` over $\mathbb{C}$ (the subfield of $\mathbb{C}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{C}$ by the coefficientwise images of the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the expansions $\mathrm{qExpand}_{\mathbb{Q}}\, d\, j_q$ for $d \mid N$, $d \neq 0$), each place being a valuation subring containing $\mathbb{C}$, proper, with principal ideals, together with positive ramification indices $e_\tau$, such that $P_{\gamma\tau} = P_\tau$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(N)$, such that $x$ lies in the valuation subring of $P_\tau$ exactly when $\lVert \mathrm{realize}\, N\, x\rVert$ is bounded along the punctured neighbourhood filter of $\tau$ in $\mathbb{H}$, and such that for $x \neq 0$ the meromorphic order at $\tau$ of $z \mapsto \mathrm{realize}\, N\, x\, (\mathrm{ofComplex}\, z)$ equals $e_\tau \cdot \mathrm{ord}_{P_\tau}(x)$. Let $\tau \in \mathbb{H}$ and let $x \in \mathbb{C}F_N$ lie in the valuation subring of $P_\tau$. Then there is $g : \mathbb{C} \to \mathbb{C}$, analytic at $\tau$, such that $z \mapsto \mathrm{realize}\, N\, x\, (\mathrm{ofComplex}\, z)$ agrees with $g$ on a punctured neighbourhood of $\tau$ and $g(\tau) = \mathrm{evalAt}_{P_\tau}(x)$, the latter being the preimage in $\mathbb{C}$ of the residue class of $x$ in the residue field of $P_\tau$. Here $\mathrm{realize}\, N\, x\, \sigma$ is $g_0(\sigma)/h_0(\sigma)$ for some chosen pair of modular forms $g_0, h_0$ of equal weight on $\Gamma_0(N)$ with $h_0(\sigma) \neq 0$ and $x \cdot \mathrm{qExpansion}(h_0) = \mathrm{qExpansion}(g_0)$, and $0$ if no such pair exists.
--
--   This is the removable-singularity link between the analytic and the algebraic side of the dictionary between points of $\Gamma_0(N)\backslash\mathbb{H}$ and places of the complex modular function field: a function regular at $P_\tau$ has bounded, hence analytically extendable, realisation near $\tau$, and the extended value at $\tau$ is the residue-class value of $x$ at the place. It is used in the estimates on hyperplane sections and on values of sections in the study of $J_0(N)$, for instance [`ModularCurve.JZero.exists_hyperplaneSection_defect_le`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZero.exists_hyperplaneSection_defect_le) and [`ModularCurve.JZero.exists_log_secVal_sub_le`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZero.exists_log_secVal_sub_le).
